A||||18||Songman||First lawsuits in Nashville Greyhound crash||||1||
Z||000000||Songman||08-23-2001||09:01 PM||||The crash happened just North of Nashville a few days ago. 45 people injured. Some critically. One dead. The driver had an illegal license and some passengers say they had argued with him as he was falling asleep.<P>It was just a matter of time before the lawsuits started. The first one is from a mother of two children that were on the bus. She is suing Greyhound for $50 million dollars. Could this be the end of Greyhound if all of the passengers follow suit?<P>Here is one article on the crash. <A HREF="http://www.msnbc.com/news/616169.asp?cp1=1" TARGET=_blank>http://www.msnbc.com/news/616169.asp?cp1=1</A> <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||08-23-2001||09:08 PM||||Ick. That gets sticky. I wish that people didn't keep throwing around the monetary law-suits. Maybe it's just me, but your two children are dead, and all you can think of is $50M?!? Makes me ill.||||reg||13
Z||000002||Mach10||08-23-2001||09:19 PM||||Oops, I misread. Not everyone died. So I'm assuming that the children were injured. That makes it even MORE greed-oriented. $50M?!? Surely hospital/therapy bills don't run that high? <BR>Am I the only one for whom it appears that this is a cash-grab? <BR>Not to belittle the injuries and pain the children are experiencing, and the fact that someone WILL have to pay for their treatment. I fully expect Greyhound to pay for that WITHOUT a court-case. But on the other hand, it seems that everytime something happens in the US, there are people jumping ALL over it, trying to make a buck. ||||reg||11
Z||000003||JSocha||08-23-2001||10:28 PM||||&lt;takes out notepad and pen&gt;<P><B><u>Note to self:</u></B><P><FONT SIZE="3"><B>SELF!</B></FONT>  Do not board Greyhound buses in Tennessee - <I>period!</I><P>&lt;puts notepad and pen away&gt;<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||9
Z||000004||8Ball||08-24-2001||12:10 AM||||heck with that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I think I will go hop on one right now maybe I can get lucky be in a crash and solve ALL my finacial probs at once hehehehe j/k<P>Randy||||reg||1
Z||000005||Galen||08-24-2001||04:28 AM||||Let me say this... DAMN!... I'm with Mach, greedy ass parents. I admit if I had kids(which I never will <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) and if they were on a greyhound bus(which they never will be) and the bus wrecked. I would be a lil unhappy with greyhound, but 50mill? shoot.. I'd make a deal with a greyhound driver..<P>"hey man, I'm gonna be on this bus, wreck it but dont kill me and i'l give ya cool 10mill"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>United States of the Overly Annoying and Stupid women who want too much damned money for a greyhound crash.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">  Ray -    <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>    - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000006||84Bill||08-24-2001||07:44 AM||||A NJ casino bus flipped over just the other day. Apparently the driver was going to fast and had to swerve off the road to avoid hitting stopped cars. Seems to be a rash of theese lately||||reg||1
Z||000007||WampusCat||08-24-2001||08:02 AM||||A Florida jury just awarded $480,000,000 to three people who were injured in the 1989 crash of a Cessna 185.  Wonder if this will be the second time the light plane industry gets killed off due to lawsuits.  <A HREF="http://www.aopa.org/whatsnew/newsitems/2001/01-3-051x.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.aopa.org/whatsnew/newsitems/2001/01-3-051x.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||84Bill||08-24-2001||09:12 AM||||I've had that happen to me in a Grumman and I can tell you if my instructor had not acted quickly we would have made a nice paisly runway covering. Since then I ALWAYS check my seat by rocking back and forth as hard as I can just to be sure it's locked in. <BR>This Cessna had it's rail(s) replaced and it still slipped out of it's lock. I would first look into the maintainence records to see if this rail was inspected properly then question the pilot in command. Cessna should ammend its prestart checklist to include the importance of checking the seat for positive lock but that costs money  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR>I'm not sure if it is part of the check list for a 182 but it should be in ALL aircraft since they all share a simillar design.<BR>480 mil is a bit extreme.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Mach10||08-25-2001||01:36 PM||||Reminds me of a bumpersticker I saw. It's funny, but has serious social implications:<P>"Go Ahead, Tailgate me. Then I'll slam on my brakes, and sue you"<P>This does not bode well. No wonder the US economy is flopping. All the money's being diverted out of industry and into crash-victims, clumsy-ass people who fell down stairs, and the owners of the multitude of boxes of small kittens.<P>Come up to Canada. You rear-end me, I punch you in the nose, and start an insurance claim. End of story. Everyone's happy.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Galen||08-25-2001||03:28 PM||||gotta love a country where someone touches ya car, ya beat the living snot out of em..<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">  Ray -    <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>    - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000011||EdsB52||08-26-2001||02:12 AM||||Civil litigation is present in our society to present deterrence to people, corporations, and sometimes government (although they have self-given immunity from civil prosecution) from acting irresponsibly. Criminal jeopardy is present to prevent deterrence to people and corporations (although criminal convictions almost always result in civil penalty) from committing the most heinous behavior in our society. But we can't consciously jail people for hitting a parked car by accident, with no human physical injuries, when not impaired. It's not rational due to its cruel nature. For actions that don't qualify for criminal jeopardy, we need to establish a process of relief so people don't resort to taking the law into their own hands.<P>Tort limits, like the ones being established by our current administration, work against the dissuasive properties of civil jeopardy. In regard to HMO's, it may be more 'cost effective' to neglect a patients needs and pay the maximum damage. If no limits, or reasonably higher limits were established, corporations would act more responsibly. I'll bet every person that might disagree with me would waffle if it were his or her loved one(s) negligently murdered by a corporate act of 'cost effectiveness.' Most people realize it will never be them in those shoes so it doesn't matter. Remember think about equal protection.<P>So if we subscribe to the Neanderthal practice of beating the crap out of someone when we feel they've offended us, then the bigger you are the more right you are. Sounds like the old western days where the fastest draw wins regardless of law. That means women have no rights because they can't beat the crap out of anyone. This principal might sound good to some on paper, but it doesn't accomplish one of the things the law sets out to do, and that's to protect those that cannot protect themselves. I agree that 50 million is too high, but let's let the court determine that.<P>“Cessna should ammend its prestart checklist to include the importance of checking the seat for positive lock but that costs money  ”<P>I agree. Responsible behavior has mutuality and reciprocity. Being a pilot myself, I think more culpability should reside with the pilot. Any pilot that’s worth his or her salt knows those seat rails suck and wear to the point of breakage or, as in this case, have the stops fall/break off. The preflight checklist includes the inspection of all flight control surfaces, landing gear, tires, brakes, engine, and many other items; are Cessna and the FAA (organization that certifies aircraft) saying that the seat rails only require inspection at 100 hour and/or annual inspections? Hey Bill, do you still fly? If so, in what capacity? I’m a big fan of homebuilt aircraft largely because of this litigation that threatens to eliminate a cool sport. With homebuilt aircraft, you, the builder becomes the manufacturer, even if you purchased a kit (must be less than 50% completed by the manufacturer of the kit to qualify). Do you fly WampusCat?||||reg||1
Z||000012||Galen||08-26-2001||06:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by EdsB52:<BR><B>That means women have no rights because they can't beat the crap out of anyone. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I can feel some harsh words coming for you man. Not saying I feel for ya, cuz you do talk to much. Get em girls<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">   Ray -     <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>     - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A> - AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000013||EdsB52||08-26-2001||07:28 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B> I can feel some harsh words coming for you man. Not saying I feel for ya, cuz you do talk to much. Get em girls<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I doubt it. Who, in your opinion did I offend? I doubt I offended any girls in this forum. In fact, they probably agree with my sentiments of violence not being the accepted process of rectifying differences. I doubt they'll openly agree with me as it's not fashionable in this forum, but that doesn't mean they disagree with me. Women, and other disadvantaged groups have been fighting the male dominated establishment for centuries, so I don't think your weak attempt at turning them against me will succeed. Do you realize that women couldn't vote in America for about 50 years after black males were legally allowed to? <P>As for talking (writing) too much; I'll take your concern under advisement. Until then, keep writing your cogent one-liners.||||reg||1
Z||000014||AusFiero||08-26-2001||10:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B> I can feel some harsh words coming for you man. Not saying I feel for ya, cuz you do talk to much. Get em girls<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>You actually read Eds posts Galen? Sheez I just see too many words and go into brain overload most of the time.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000015||Songman||08-26-2001||10:27 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B> <BR>You actually read Eds posts Galen? Sheez I just see too many words and go into brain overload most of the time.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I read part of it. What I got from it is that Ed doesn't see any problem with all of the frivilous lawsuits that are ruining this country. The lawsuits that make our insurance and doctor bills so high. The lawsuits that make any idiot who spills coffee think he has the right to $100 million...<P>But then I got bored with it and moved on down to Galen's post.. A man of few words, but usually good ones... hehe<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000016||DRH||08-26-2001||10:56 AM||||Ed said:<BR>"I agree that 50 million is too high, but let's let the court determine that."<P>I think the problem is we are letting 12 people have their sympathetic side played on to arrive at these ridiculous figures. Damages should be limited to actual damages plus reasonable attorney fees. As morbid as it may sound we should have a preset value placed on a life also. The 'logic' that the value of a life is not measurable but MUST be very, very high is ridiculous.<P>Also, if punitive damages are called for they should go to society not one victim.<P><BR>Edit to give credit to the author of the quote.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 08-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||84Bill||08-26-2001||11:18 AM||||No Ed I have not flown in a few years. Last check of my log book shows 28 hours tt. I had just started my nite flying when I left Florida and never jumped back into it. I have been around aircraft all my life since my father was a pilot.<P>I was an aircraft mechanic for a few years and got alot of heat for finding things wrong like cracked landing gear trundle lugs, you know how expensive they are to replace? I quit simply because I could not "overlook" things like that. I have replaced several seat rails during that time as well  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> What really got me was when I was told to "Stop looking so hard" when doing my inspections.<P>As far as homebuilt aircraft I think they are cool but the problem is it takes money away from the big manufacturers of the popular aircraft and they don't like that very much. not to mention "any" joe smoe can build one regardless of his or her ability and that kinda bothers me but they still get inspected (hopefully) by a competent inspector prior to certification.<P>TORT HA!!! I love that one! Here is my take on "tort" If 2 cars are involved in an incident and both are insured by Company A insurance (prior to tort) then the insurance company has a big loss on their hands if there is a large settlement. So they came up with TORT as a method to limit their loss and get more money from those that opt for the ability to file suit against one of their insured by their own insured or another companies insured driver thus limiting the insurance companies liability to pay. Insurance companies are money grubbers in the worst way. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Galen||08-26-2001||04:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by EdsB52:<BR><B> I doubt it. Who, in your opinion did I offend? I doubt I offended any girls in this forum. In fact, they probably agree with my sentiments of violence not being the accepted process of rectifying differences. I doubt they'll openly agree with me as it's not fashionable in this forum, but that doesn't mean they disagree with me. Women, and other disadvantaged groups have been fighting the male dominated establishment for centuries, so I don't think your weak attempt at turning them against me will succeed. Do you realize that women couldn't vote in America for about 50 years after black males were legally allowed to? <P>As for talking (writing) too much; I'll take your concern under advisement. Until then, keep writing your cogent one-liners.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>From what I took from that, you said women are weak, men are not. Which in my opinion, and in many others I'm sure is offensive. Evenmore so than your constant babbling. <P>One liners? You probably thing W is stoopid dont ya?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">   Ray -     <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>     - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A> - AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
